<title>NEW ZEALAND: AMP's Ergo cuts NZ two and three-year fixed rates.</title>
<headline>AMP's Ergo cuts NZ two and three-year fixed rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMP New Zealand's telephone banking subsidiary Ergo Personal Financial Services said on Thursday it was cutting its two and three-year fixed interest mortgage rates to 9.5 percent from 9.75 and 10.25 percent respectively.</p>
<p>The one-year rate remains at 9.95 percent and the floating rate at 11.25 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;A drop in wholesale rates combined with our lower cost structures (compared to the major banks) have made it possible to review our rates and pass on these additional savings to customers,&quot; Managing Director Graham Meyer said.  </p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
